---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="AMAKEUR｜野造 — independent digital studio founded by a non-programmer. Amateur at code. Serious about making."
>
  <article class="container-site py-12 sm:py-16">
    <header class="measure mx-auto mb-10 animate-fade-up">
      <p class="mb-2 text-[12px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--color-fg-subtle)]">
        Studio
      </p>
      <h1 class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-4xl tracking-[-0.03em] sm:text-5xl">
        About AMAKEUR｜野造
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-amakeur measure mx-auto animate-fade-up delay-1">
      <p>
        <strong>AMAKEUR｜野造</strong> is an independent digital studio founded by someone who does not
        primarily write code. The name is intentional: <em>amateur</em> as in lover of the craft —
        not as an apology.
      </p>
      <p>
        We ship software, games, websites, tools, and unnamed experiments. The method is unorthodox
        on purpose: natural language, AI, aesthetics, curiosity, and a bit of wild-path energy
        （野造）. If a thing wants to exist, we find a way to make it — without waiting for
        permission from a programming degree.
      </p>
      <h2>I don't code. I make.</h2>
      <p>
        Coding is one instrument. Making is the practice. We care about the feeling of a product —
        the silence between interactions, the honesty of a sentence, the small delight that doesn't
        need a changelog.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Amateur at code. Serious about making.</strong> That is not a slogan to soften
        expectations. It is a filter: we would rather ship something slightly imperfect and alive
        than something polished and empty.
      </p>
      <h2>What we work on</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/apps">Apps</a> — private utilities and quiet software</li>
        <li><a href="/games">Games</a> — playable sketches of ordinary life</li>
        <li><a href="/web">Web</a> — interactive and experimental sites</li>
        <li><a href="/labs">Labs</a> — vibecoding without a category</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Voice</h2>
      <p>
        Honest. Craft-serious. Slightly self-deprecating. Chinese and English both welcome.
        No AI-slop marketing. No fake scarcity. If we don't know yet, we say so.
      </p>
      <p>
        Production home: <a href="https://amakeur.com">{SITE.domain}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
